# SABOTAGE: THE DEV SEED'S ROLLING `aud_event` WINDOW LOSES THE CURRENT MONTH —
# `PartitionManager.ensure_rolling_partitions/2` walks `1..months_ahead` instead of
# `0..months_ahead`. The seed still prints "Seeded …" and every seeded row still writes,
# so nothing looks wrong; but the window it installs now starts NEXT month. A fresh
# checkout migrated past the launch month has no partition for today, and the FIRST audit
# write after seeding — opening an impersonation session for a drill-in, a reveal, an
# erasure — fails with `23514 no partition of relation aud_event`, exactly the
# fresh-checkout breakage the seed call exists to prevent.
#
# Aimed at the WINDOW, not at the writer: `ensure_partition/2` still creates what it is
# given, the create is still idempotent and create-only (no detach/drop), and the daily
# cron's `perform/1` still rolls forward from `0` — only the seed's own path is wrong.
#
# No warning is introduced (the walk simply starts one month later) and the replay runs
# `mix test`, so nothing is confined or skipped.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/aud_event_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: installs the previous+current+next window a dev seed needs
# MUST_FAIL: never reaches BEHIND
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/audit_event/partition_manager.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/audit_event/partition_manager.ex
@@ -266,7 +266,7 @@
 
     back = if months_back > 0, do: Enum.map(1..months_back, &shift_month(anchor, -&1)), else: []
 
-    (back ++ Enum.map(0..months_ahead, &shift_month(anchor, &1)))
+    (back ++ Enum.map(1..months_ahead, &shift_month(anchor, &1)))
     |> Enum.map(&first_of_month/1)
     |> Enum.uniq()
     |> Enum.map(&ensure_partition(repo, &1))
